      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'm trying to finalize this monthly reconciliation macro and I've hit a wall. I keep getting a run-time error '1004': application-defined or object-defined error on this line:\n\nSub MonthlyRecon()\n    Dim ws As Worksheet\n    Set ws = ThisWorkbook.Sheets(\"Monthly_Report\")\n    ws.Range(\"A1:Z100\").Value = DataArray\n    ws.Columns(\"A:Z\").AutoFit\nEnd Sub\n\nThe DataArray is definitely dimensioned correctly and populated, so I can't figure out why Excel is rejecting the assignment. It's a really strange bug—the code runs fine most of the time, but then it suddenly acts up and throws this error out of nowhere like it's being erratic. Can you look at the syntax and tell me why this specific range assignment is failing?",
